WEBVTT

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:10.260
<i>Present day high school student Saburo 
is taken back in time to the Warring States period.</i>

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:14.030
Oh, yeah! You look like me.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.950
Be my decoy!

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.950
<i>He aims to rule Japan 
as Nobunaga Oda.</i>

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.500
We're only after one man:

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.120
General Yoshimoto Imagawa!

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:26.540
<i>On the one hand,</i>

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:30.330
<i>it created surprising encounters with others 
who had also been sent back from the present.</i>

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.720
<i>Namely, an ex-cop and an ex-yakuza.</i>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:37.930
Beginning today, our enemy is

00:00:40.270 --> 00:00:41.390
Nobunaga Oda!

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.890
You cannot defeat my brother.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.880
Brother!

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:47.880
<i>On the other hand, it caused 
undesirable conflicts.</i>

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.730
You know, I thought the closer 
you got to conquering Japan,

00:00:51.730 --> 00:00:54.530
the fewer enemies there'd be.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.170
<i>Rule the land.</i>

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:06.080
It was a long, arduous path that 
tore him apart from his beloved retainers.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.360
Hey, sorry for the wait.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:20.540
My lord, today is 
an auspicious day—

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:23.680
My lord, I commend you for your 
efforts in the latest battle.

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:25.620
Yeah.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:30.140
We have fully accepted 
our father's death.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:34.190
I am proud to know that my 
father was of help to you.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.490
Yeah.

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:44.900
So I'm thinking of having 
the four of you work here as pages.

00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.700
Yes! I am grateful.

00:01:48.250 --> 00:01:50.880
Ranmaru, Boumaru, Rikimaru.

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:55.460
I would like these three to be 
by your side as pages.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:01:58.150
And you, the big brother?

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:03.760
I come today to ask if you may allow me to 
immediately finish my coming-of-age ceremony

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:05.460
and become the head 
of the Mori family.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:09.790
All right. Sure.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:14.980
Succeed the Mori family and 
serve me as a general.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:16.780
Yes, sir!

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:19.310
My lord.

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:27.450
What? Again?

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:31.000
My lord, is it another enemy?

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.300
Nah, not an enemy. An oni.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.090
Oni?

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:40.930
Well, I'm not sure if it's true or not,
 but I totally want to see it if it is.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:44.510
Allow me, then, to hunt it down.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.340
An oni hunt?

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.930
Like Momotaro!

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:49.850
Momotaro?

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:56.160
Oh, yeah! You look Momotaro-ish, 
with your chiseled face.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.400
Totally, oni hunt!

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.430
I will go, too.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.450
Me too.

00:03:02.030 --> 00:03:04.580
Awesome, Mori Brothers!

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.410
Hey, and there's exactly four of you!

00:03:07.730 --> 00:03:11.530
Respectfully, I cannot 
participate in an oni hunt.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.670
I do not have confidence 
in my ability.

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.250
Oh.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:19.780
What should we do, then?

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:22.050
We don't have the dog.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:23.770
Dog.

00:03:24.590 --> 00:03:26.040
Dog. Oh!

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:28.970
What? Oh, arf.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:33.040
My lord, I have caught the oni!

00:03:34.390 --> 00:03:38.460
Huh? It's just a black dude.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.680
Wait, those clothes…

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:46.080
And it's a bat.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.160
<b>HOME RUN KING</b>

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.160
<b>Fifth 
year 
straight</b>

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.160
<b>YOUNG</b>

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:49.620
Young!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.910
The professional baseball player!

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:53.060
The five-year home run king!

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:53.920
Young! It's you!

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.670
My lord, do you know this man?

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:05.430
Impressive, my lord! You forced him 
into surrender so quickly!

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:07.930
I see.

00:04:08.570 --> 00:04:10.680
So we got sent back from 
around the same time.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.770
Although not to the same time.

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.000
Yes.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:20.220
I don't know anything anymore.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:25.150
Lightning struck during a game,

00:04:25.150 --> 00:04:30.160
and when I came to, 
I was collapsed on the beach.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:32.910
My team's in Saitama,

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:36.540
so I was like, huh, there's 
no water in Saitama.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:37.630
It was a shock!

00:04:38.080 --> 00:04:39.950
I can imagine.

00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:41.880
You'd totally be shocked.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:45.590
You wouldn't think you'd get 
sent back in time, would you?

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:48.030
It was so awful.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:52.430
I'm so happy I met someone

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.250
that knows me.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.640
I'm happy, too.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:01.360
I never thought I'd meet 
the home run king here.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:09.280
But why did we slip back in time?

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:11.510
Dunno.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:15.290
I guess it's like 
being in an accident.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:18.490
I don't know how to 
fix it or anything,

00:05:18.490 --> 00:05:22.090
so we'll just have to do our 
best to live in this age.

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.100
You're—

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:29.680
You're kind of goofy.

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:33.120
No way.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:39.320
<i>Young was later given 
the name Yasuke.</i>

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.170
<i>He came to serve as 
Saburo's bodyguard.</i>

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:51.280
My lord, Happy New Year.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:54.310
Yeah. Happy New Year.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:57.040
Oh, yeah! 
Micchi, do you want some soup?

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:14.500
You know something?

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:16.420
We're getting old.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:22.920
I'm always tired, 
no matter how much I rest.

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:26.530
Y'know, we were warring 
non-stop last year.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:29.030
We were in a pinch so many times.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.240
I'm so tired.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:35.250
And then the New Year season 
gets really busy, too.

00:06:35.960 --> 00:06:40.340
Well then, how about you 
go outside by yourself for a change?

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:43.880
You used to do it 
all the time, I hear.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:48.620
Yeah, but there might be more 
people coming to greet me.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:49.650
Saburo.

00:06:52.620 --> 00:06:54.620
Have you forgotten what I look like?

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:03.970
My lord.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:08.420
What is the matter?

00:07:09.390 --> 00:07:11.360
You look pale.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:12.720
Kichou.

00:07:12.720 --> 00:07:15.260
You were so well until just earlier.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:19.200
Did you eat something suspicious?

00:07:19.570 --> 00:07:25.000
No, I am actually feeling 
particularly good today.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:29.180
My lord, please get some rest.

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:33.320
You must be tired.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:38.060
I would not like you to become 
sickly again, as you used to be.

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:41.790
Kichou.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:45.980
Did you hate how I was before?

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.120
Hate you?

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:56.720
I was just lonely.

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:02.120
Sorry, Kichou.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:07.470
I have always wanted to apologize.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:09.310
I am sorry.

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:12.810
My lord.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:17.110
You must be feeling really bad.

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:20.170
For you to suddenly bring that up.

00:08:21.130 --> 00:08:23.900
You are not yourself.

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:26.990
I suppose not.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:38.610
Ever since you became healthy, 
I have never felt lonely.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:44.460
I have been happy
 far more often than not.

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:47.820
I see.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:02.800
It's relaxing being up high.

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:08.580
Yo, Nobunaga.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:13.340
I came all this way 
in the cold for you.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:16.610
<i>Why does this man always 
have such an attitude?</i>

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.000
What's wrong?

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.690
Aren't you going to at 
least say something kind?

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:23.620
Thank you for coming 
despite this cold weather.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:25.160
You must be tired.

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:27.710
What's your problem?

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:30.440
Why are you being so 
polite now? Creep.

00:09:30.440 --> 00:09:32.380
Are you messing with me?

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:34.130
<i>What is wrong with this man?</i>

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:35.800
<i>I do not understand.</i>

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:41.740
Damn, man, you've had it rough 
this last year, huh?

00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:44.180
That's what you get.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.690
It's interesting, though, 
the Warring States age.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:55.440
There is so much more to live for than 
our Japan a few hundred years from now.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.610
<b>A few hundred years?</b>

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:59.940
<i>Japan a few hundred years from now?</i>

00:09:59.940 --> 00:10:02.410
Don't you think, Nobunaga?

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:04.160
<b>A few hundred years...</b>

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.160
<i>A few hundred years from now...</i>

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:07.230
So, what's your plan now?

00:10:07.230 --> 00:10:10.300
Enryaku-ji of Mount Hiei and
Hongan-ji of Ishiyama.

00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:12.980
Those kinds of men are trouble.

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:14.170
<b>Japan?</b>

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.170
Japan?

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:18.600
They're protected by extraterritorial 
rights, and they're armed.

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:21.230
They're worse than yakuza.

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:24.100
Yo, are you listening to me, asshole?

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:24.310
<b>Japan, a few hundred years from now...</b>

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:30.690
I see. I am convinced.

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:34.650
Are you feeling sick or something?

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:36.680
Or are the holidays making you lazy?

00:10:36.680 --> 00:10:39.610
Do not worry about me,
 Matsunaga-dono.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.060
I'm not worried.

00:10:42.060 --> 00:10:44.720
No matter who I am against,

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:50.540
I will exert myself to the fullest 
for the Oda family.

00:10:59.020 --> 00:11:00.650
Hashiba-dono.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:04.710
I hear that you defeated 
the Azai army with a small force

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:09.160
when they attacked our castles 
in Yokoyama and Hashiba.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:10.530
Oh, well...

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:14.270
I am honored to receive your praise.

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:17.280
My lord, are we not attacking Azai?

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:22.160
I doubt Azai has any 
strength right now.

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:26.330
Might we not be able to take even 
the heavily-defended castle in Odani?

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.290
No.

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.970
Azai still has Asakura behind them.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:31.950
It would not be easy.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:36.340
The trouble is the uprising 
being inspired by Ishiyama Hongan-ji.

00:11:36.700 --> 00:11:40.630
We must suppress them before we 
can spend any more men or time on this.

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:42.760
I am concerned about 
Takeda's actions, as well.

00:11:43.570 --> 00:11:46.870
Mount Hiei is an enemy now, too.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:52.890
We've still got so many enemies.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:10.100
It has been a long time, Takugen.

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:15.380
Perhaps it is strange that I ask 
you this, as you are a priest.

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:19.000
What do you think of 
Enryaku-ji of Mount Hiei?

00:12:19.480 --> 00:12:25.240
I believe it is the highest Buddhist 
temple, with a long history.

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:30.950
But I have not heard good things 
about it in a long time.

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:36.190
Slacking on training, breaking abstinence, 
going to war and killing.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:39.070
Would you approve of 
their destruction?

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:43.030
What are you planning, 
Mitsuhide-sama?

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.720
I simply want

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:50.950
to reduce the number of my enemies.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:59.080
But despite its corruption,
there are many who respect its authority.

00:12:59.080 --> 00:13:01.260
If you were to defeat them,

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:05.200
you would inevitably be seen 
as an enemy of the Buddha.

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:12.290
Is that man — Nobunaga Oda — 
prepared for that?

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:27.090
It stopped.

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:27.970
Yes.

00:13:32.630 --> 00:13:34.580
Micchi, what's up?

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:39.080
My lord, I would like to discuss 
something with you in private.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:45.130
My lord, are you serious?

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:49.610
Yep. We're attacking 
Enryaku-ji of Mount Hiei.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:57.050
But my lord, Mount Hiei has 
extraterritorial rights.

00:13:57.050 --> 00:14:00.920
To attack them would be to 
go against the peace.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.570
We may receive backlash from 
other daimyos and citizens.

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:06.060
I guess.

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:11.580
I don't like it when the people hate me, 
but the daimyos hate me already anyway.

00:14:12.020 --> 00:14:12.740
But —

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:14.200
I am in favor of it!

00:14:15.520 --> 00:14:20.170
My father was killed by Azai and Asakura, 
and the monk soldiers of Enryaku-ji.

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:23.740
I do not care about so-called 
extraterritorial rights.

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:27.800
We cannot allow them 
to remain in safety!

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:30.900
Nagayoshi!

00:14:30.900 --> 00:14:33.020
Do not shout at the lord.

00:14:36.260 --> 00:14:40.170
I am therefore in favor of 
attacking Enryaku-ji.

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:43.570
What reason is there to disagree?

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:46.990
The lord aspires to take all of Japan.

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:50.030
Everyone that stands in his way

00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:53.240
must be eliminated.

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:56.190
Indeed.

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:59.360
It is Japan itself that we want.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:03.040
Enryaku-ji is not worth fearing.

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:08.420
It would scare Ishiyama Hongan-ji, 
since they're another religious force.

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:15.300
I suspect the lord has already 
made up his mind to attack Enryaku-ji.

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:18.830
I doubt we could change his mind.

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:20.400
In that case...

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:24.050
we will have to prepare 
for the worst.

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:31.950
Looks like you're all on board.

00:15:33.220 --> 00:15:36.220
Okay, Micchi is going to be 
the supreme general.

00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:36.950
Thanks.

00:15:38.860 --> 00:15:40.010
Yes, sir.

00:15:40.010 --> 00:15:42.620
I will take care of it, my lord.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:55.490
What is going on so early 
in the morning?

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:11.580
Oda!

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:12.650
It's Oda!

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.290
Oda is attacking us!

00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:16.760
Oda?

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:19.290
What nonsense is this?

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.500
They have already surrounded 
the foot of the mountain!

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:26.040
Impossible.

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:31.380
An attack on Mount Hiei 
is unconscionable.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.740
Do not let the monk soldiers escape!

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:38.050
Cut down every last one of them!

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:44.810
<i>I was not sure about allowing him 
to fight on the front lines,</i>

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:47.690
<i>no matter what he desired.</i>

00:16:47.990 --> 00:16:51.020
<i>But, indeed, he is a warrior 
like his father.</i>

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:53.030
I will not spare monk soldiers.

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:57.120
Are you in your right minds?

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:59.990
This land is governed by the Buddha.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:01.620
Do you intend to taint it with blood?

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:06.640
So you say that the blood of a monk 
serving the Buddha is tainted?

00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:09.250
I am speaking of you, 
barbaric samurai!

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:12.570
Then never fear!

00:17:12.570 --> 00:17:17.100
It is the blood of you monks 
that will be spilt!

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:22.200
This is the nature of war.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:23.800
If you did not want to die,

00:17:23.800 --> 00:17:27.310
you should have never meddled 
in the wars of the samurai.

00:17:38.230 --> 00:17:42.410
This is an act of sacrilege 
against the Buddha.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:46.890
Nobunaga is the Devil King 
of the Sixth Heaven.

00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:52.850
He will surely receive 
Buddha's punishment.

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:04.110
<i>The Devil King of the Sixth Heaven,
who fears not even the Buddha himself...</i>

00:18:07.720 --> 00:18:11.370
<i>I will take that name.</i>

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:16.370
Mount Hiei is burning.

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:20.660
Akechi-dono is more than he appears.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.450
Magnificent.

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:26.490
Serves them right. 
Damn priests.

00:18:26.490 --> 00:18:29.760
This is what they get for 
opposing the Oda family.

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:33.170
I wish I could be there, too.

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:37.370
I wanted to see the looks 
on their faces as they fled.

00:18:37.370 --> 00:18:38.760
I agree.

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:45.010
Nobunaga-san.

00:18:48.160 --> 00:18:51.850
This place you live in is terrifying.

00:18:56.940 --> 00:18:58.800
It's the Warring States period, after all.

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:27.680
<i>I do not know why.</i>

00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:39.280
<i>Why he suddenly came 
raining on top of me.</i>

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:52.340
<i>All I know is that his presence 
saved me and the Oda family.</i>

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:58.240
<i>Saburo...</i>

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:03.640
<i>I suspect I was, in some ways,</i>

00:20:04.470 --> 00:20:07.100
<i>afraid of knowing who you truly are.</i>

00:20:09.820 --> 00:20:12.200
<i>Japan a few hundred years from now...</i>

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:22.990
You come from quite a far-off place.

00:20:27.440 --> 00:20:28.490
What?

00:20:28.940 --> 00:20:30.500
What are you talking about?

00:20:36.720 --> 00:20:37.890
Nothing.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:47.420
Saburo, I will live for you alone.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:21:00.740
That's going a little too far.

00:21:07.300 --> 00:21:12.260
<i>And so the true concerto 
of the two Nobunagas</i>

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:14.160
<i>has now begun.</i>

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.480
<b>Episode 10</b>

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:23.480
<b>The Two Nobunagas</b>

00:21:23.480 --> 00:21:25.480
<b></b>
